<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johann Wilhelm Ludwig Gleim</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1719">1719</a>–<a href="/years/1803">1803</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Johann Wilhelm Ludwig Gleim was a German poet of the Anacreontic school who served from 1747 as secretary of the cathedral chapter at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/halberstadt">Halberstadt</a>. His patriotic Prussian war songs, written in the voice of a grenadier, celebrated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-the-great">Frederick the Great</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a>, and he was a generous friend and correspondent of many writers. His house in Halberstadt, the Gleimhaus, is now a literary museum.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/johann-wilhelm-ludwig-gleim.jpg" alt="Johann Wilhelm Ludwig Gleim" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GleimJWL.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
